ock number to get the full 14 bits of disk storage.  remember, OS/8 needs to get the one bit of cheating and even then that only gets you half way!  The P?S/8 system handler will get the first 4096 blocks of all 8 of them, and the non-system handlers can access up to block 31277.  Larger on still larger devices such as the MDC8.\line\line So, when this is done, it will be quite useful IF the serial connection is decent speed.  And in any case, P?S/8 is lower-overhead so it will outperform OS/8 on most things as is usual.\par
